<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea seeks 40,000 tonnes of U.S. No.1 soybean.</title>
<headline>S.Korea seeks 40,000 tonnes of U.S. No.1 soybean.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's state-run Agricultural &amp; Fishery Marketing Corp (AFMC) said on Tuesday it will invite tenders for 40,000 tonnes of U.S. No.1 soybean on January 29.  </p>
<p>An official at the corporation said it will close the bids by 4:00 p.m. (0700 GMT) on January 28.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:</p>
<p> POSITION  TONNE	     SHIPMENT		   ARRIVAL/PORT</p>
<p>			 U.S. GULF	U.S. PNW</p>
<p>  ONE     20,000   Jan 30-Feb 18  Feb 14-Mar 5   Mar 25/Inchon</p>
<p>  TWO     20,000   Feb 24-Mar 15  Mar 11-30	Apr 20/Inchon</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
